    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d336">

                <pb facs="0486" n="390" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg390"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.51/1347c</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dearing</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to President King</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-11-09"><hi rendition="#italic">November 9,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: The copy of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">pro forma</hi> Budget transmitted as an enclosure of the
                    letter dated November 4, 1921,<anchor n="12" xml:id="d336-f1"/> addressed to me
                    at your direction by Mr. Dennis, Secretary of the Commission, has been
                    received.</p>
                <p>The understanding that the current administrative expenses of the Liberian
                    Government shall not in any year during the operation of the loan exceed
                    $270,000 per annum is hereby confirmed.</p>
                <p>Before enactment this Budget and those to be prepared annually hereafter, in
                    keeping with the provisions of the loan plan, will have to receive within the
                    limit of the aforesaid $270,000 agreed upon, the formal approval of the
                    Financial Commissioner as to its items. Any Budget so approved is not subject to
                    change. However, the Department is of the opinion that the Budget of the first
                    year would, in all probability, be approved by the Financial Commissioner since
                    it has the sanction of the Department.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. M. Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
